From: user <user@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: apply the core clock rate after enabling it

RPM-backed clocks (the qcom,clk-smd-rpm provider used on MSM8998, SDM660
and friends) silently ignore clk_set_rate() while the clock is disabled:

    static int clk_smd_rpm_set_rate(struct clk_hw *hw, unsigned long rate,
                                    unsigned long parent_rate)
    {
            ...
            if (!r->enabled)
                    return 0;
            ...
    }

ipa_power_init() requests the IPA core clock rate before the clock has
ever been enabled, so on those platforms the rate is never programmed
and the clock keeps its default rate.  On SDM660 this is visible as
clk_get_rate() returning INT_MAX (the rpmcc default) even right after a
successful clk_set_rate() call.

Re-apply the requested rate in ipa_power_enable(), immediately after the
core clock has been enabled, so the rate actually reaches the RPM.  The
early request in ipa_power_init() is kept so clock providers that accept
it before enable keep working as before.

Tested on Xiaomi Mi Pad 4 (SDM660): clk_get_rate(ipa core clock) now
reports the requested 75000000 Hz instead of 2147483647.

---
 drivers/net/ipa/ipa_power.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_power.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_power.c
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@
 struct ipa_power {
 	struct device *dev;
 	struct clk *core;
+	u32 core_rate;
 	struct qmp *qmp;
 	u32 interconnect_count;
 	struct icc_bulk_data interconnect[] __counted_by(interconnect_count);
@@ -108,6 +109,19 @@
 				 power->interconnect);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * RPM-backed clocks ignore clk_set_rate() while the clock is
+	 * disabled, so the rate requested in ipa_power_init() has not
+	 * been applied yet.  Do it now that the clock is running.
+	 */
+	if (!ret && clk_get_rate(power->core) != power->core_rate) {
+		int r = clk_set_rate(power->core, power->core_rate);
+
+		if (r)
+			dev_warn(power->dev,
+				 "error %d setting core clock rate\n", r);
+	}
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -261,6 +275,7 @@
 	}
 	power->dev = dev;
 	power->core = clk;
+	power->core_rate = data->core_clock_rate;
 	power->interconnect_count = data->interconnect_count;
 
 	ret = ipa_interconnect_init(power, data->interconnect_data);
